WEBVTT

00:02.800 --> 00:04.740
This is my friend,

00:06.860 --> 00:08.200
Sora!

00:09.780 --> 00:12.720
So this is a disintegrating slime?

00:12.720 --> 00:17.790
I've been an adventurer for a long time, 
and I've never seen a slime this rare before.

00:17.790 --> 00:19.760
It's adorable.

00:22.790 --> 00:26.220
See? See? Ivy's amazing, isn't he?

00:26.220 --> 00:28.690
Why are you the one 
bragging about it, Lattrua?

00:28.690 --> 00:31.640
Because I was the one who met Ivy first!

00:31.920 --> 00:33.770
It's just so adorable!

00:35.180 --> 00:40.250
I've only ever heard of transparent 
slimes in legends and stories.

00:40.250 --> 00:42.900
And this is the first I've heard 
of an ability to pick out villains.

00:42.900 --> 00:45.030
So cute!

00:46.590 --> 00:48.940
<i>For some reason, I feel 
like Sora doesn't like that.</i>

00:47.640 --> 00:48.940
It's just so cute!

00:49.210 --> 00:51.410
Come with me, Rikvelt.

00:57.540 --> 00:59.410
It's all right. Don't mind them.

00:59.410 --> 01:02.640
Rikvelt has a weakness for adorable animals.

01:02.640 --> 01:05.590
Though they often end up hating him 
because he pets them too much.

01:11.310 --> 01:15.450
<i>When I'm alone, I can breathe</i>

01:15.450 --> 01:19.610
<i>In a world with no one 
but me, I feel at ease</i>

01:20.270 --> 01:24.630
<i>But I think the truth is</i>

01:24.630 --> 01:30.610
<i>That I've been waiting for 
morning's light to break through</i>

01:28.110 --> 01:36.370
<b>The Weakest Tamer
Began a Journey
to Pick Up Trash</b>

01:28.270 --> 01:30.610
<i>(Where could it be?)</i>

01:30.610 --> 01:33.860
<i>Beyond the edges of a yet unknown map</i>

01:33.860 --> 01:38.120
<i>That's where I'll find a place 
where I can live</i>

01:36.370 --> 01:38.120
<i>(If it exists...)</i>

01:38.120 --> 01:40.130
<i>I'd like to go there</i>

01:40.130 --> 01:43.880
<i>And with trembling legs, 
I take a step forward</i>

01:43.880 --> 01:46.470
<i>I'm on a journey without end</i>

01:46.470 --> 01:48.780
<i>And even if I carry nothing with me</i>

01:48.780 --> 01:50.930
<i>I'll take everything I feel</i>

01:50.930 --> 01:52.890
<i>And pack it into my once empty bag</i>

01:52.890 --> 01:54.710
<i>I'll go as far as I need to</i>

01:54.710 --> 01:56.930
<i>On this journey to find myself</i>

01:56.930 --> 01:59.020
<i>And everything I'm given along the way</i>

01:59.020 --> 02:03.480
<i>Will slowly fill my heart to the brim</i>

02:13.350 --> 02:17.710
<i>Now, I'm not all alone anymore</i>

02:17.710 --> 02:22.630
<i>Because I've met new, dear friends</i>

02:22.630 --> 02:27.380
<i>(Maybe we can understand each other 
because we're alike. Isn't it strange?)</i>

02:27.380 --> 02:30.590
<i>Your bright laughter gives me courage</i>

02:30.590 --> 02:34.850
<i>(I feel like I'm wrapped up 
snugly by your warmth)</i>

02:34.850 --> 02:40.100
<i>From now on, let's stay 
together forever and ever</i>

02:41.020 --> 02:46.020
<b>Toward a Confrontation
with the Organization</b>

02:47.170 --> 02:49.980
Taming a slime as rare as this one...

02:50.370 --> 02:52.600
Ivy, you're an amazing tamer!

02:52.600 --> 02:54.840
What? Um... right.

02:54.840 --> 02:58.060
And a slime that can see through 
wrongdoers is valuable indeed.

02:58.060 --> 02:59.660
Let me try it! Please?

03:00.070 --> 03:04.210
Sora, I'm Lattrua of the Blazing Sword!

03:05.470 --> 03:06.920
He's saying that's not true.

03:06.920 --> 03:09.840
Amazing! He can see through lies?

03:09.840 --> 03:14.050
No, we said your name earlier, 
so he already knew that was a lie.

03:14.050 --> 03:18.100
And he may simply be reacting 
with dislike for Rikvelt.

03:18.100 --> 03:19.680
Oh, don't say that!

03:20.110 --> 03:22.100
Then, I'll give it a try.

03:22.100 --> 03:24.140
My name is Malreek.

03:25.910 --> 03:27.480
He's saying that's not true.

03:27.480 --> 03:30.980
You're right! My name is Lokreek.

03:30.980 --> 03:35.570
That's Malreek there. Yesterday, he hid 
and secretly drank Shifale's alcohol.

03:37.160 --> 03:39.090
He's saying that's true.

03:39.090 --> 03:40.160
What?!

03:40.160 --> 03:42.420
I <i>knew</i> there was less alcohol 
left than there should be.

03:42.420 --> 03:44.950
Malreek, it was you?

03:46.540 --> 03:47.820
You're not getting away!

03:51.680 --> 03:54.130
Don't mind them. This happens all the time.

03:54.130 --> 03:56.650
He can tell what's true and what isn't.

03:57.050 --> 03:59.470
Sora, you're an amazing slime, aren't you?

04:01.300 --> 04:04.850
Yes! He's my dear friend!

04:06.540 --> 04:12.030
Still, I never imagined that the three 
from the Green Gale would be traitors.

04:12.030 --> 04:14.550
For a long time here in Otolwa,

04:14.550 --> 04:17.990
there have been kidnappings committed 
by a slave trade organization.

04:17.990 --> 04:19.680
We can't seem to find 
any information on them,

04:19.680 --> 04:22.650
and even when we do find a clue, 
they immediately elude us.

04:22.650 --> 04:23.850
We haven't gotten anywhere.

04:23.850 --> 04:28.000
If there are traitors who have been
 leaking our plans to the organization,

04:28.000 --> 04:30.070
then it all makes sense.

04:30.070 --> 04:35.750
But thanks to Ivy, we now know that Meela, 
Tolto, and Malma are the traitors.

04:35.750 --> 04:40.040
If we can capture the Green Gale, then 
it should be easier for us to take action.

04:40.040 --> 04:41.860
It's a huge accomplishment, Ivy.

04:42.290 --> 04:43.500
Right...

04:43.850 --> 04:46.160
Is it painful to think of 
Meela being a bad person?

04:46.160 --> 04:46.850
What?

04:49.150 --> 04:50.310
Yes.

04:50.920 --> 04:54.270
I feel the same way. 
We've been friends since we were kids.

04:56.230 --> 04:59.160
Rik, Malma's a good 
friend of yours, isn't he?

04:59.160 --> 05:01.750
If it's too painful for you, 
you can step away from this case.

05:02.200 --> 05:07.330
No, because he's my friend, I want 
to catch him with my own hands.

05:07.330 --> 05:08.250
I see.

05:09.890 --> 05:15.130
Um, when did this organization
 start doing bad things?

05:15.130 --> 05:17.380
It started over ten years ago.

05:17.380 --> 05:21.800
People thought that kids were going missing
because they'd fallen victim to monsters.

05:21.800 --> 05:25.360
But seven years ago, we confirmed 
the existence of an organization.

05:25.730 --> 05:29.210
We learned of it when we took some 
victims who escaped into our protection.

05:29.630 --> 05:33.480
In that case, there may be other traitors.

05:34.290 --> 05:36.880
If the organization has been 
active for that long,

05:36.880 --> 05:39.570
then I don't think it can be 
just one team of traitors.

05:39.570 --> 05:41.160
You're right.

05:42.400 --> 05:45.200
Do you remember us telling you 
about when the raid failed?

05:45.200 --> 05:49.130
Yes. You'd found their hideout 
and the Watch raided,

05:49.130 --> 05:52.100
but the information had leaked somehow.

05:52.100 --> 05:53.900
The hideout was completely deserted.

05:53.900 --> 05:57.010
And the ally of the Watch who had 
infiltrated the organization was killed.

05:57.010 --> 06:00.640
Only a handful of people knew the details 
of that undertaking ahead of time.

06:00.640 --> 06:04.180
The Green Gale would only have 
learned of it right before it happened.

06:04.550 --> 06:08.640
Which means there's a definite 
possibility that other traitors exist.

06:08.640 --> 06:10.510
That <i>is</i> a problem.

06:10.510 --> 06:14.230
The Green Gale's promotion was 
endorsed by a member of the nobility.

06:14.230 --> 06:15.770
That's why I trusted them.

06:15.770 --> 06:16.910
Endorsed?

06:16.910 --> 06:20.360
Are that noble and the 
Green Gale close friends?

06:20.800 --> 06:26.160
No. Apparently, the Green Gale solved 
a problem that the noble had.

06:26.160 --> 06:30.040
That led the noble to recommend 
their promotion to high-level adventurers.

06:30.400 --> 06:34.720
Do members of the nobility often 
recommend adventurers for promotions?

06:35.270 --> 06:37.020
No, it's unusual.

06:37.020 --> 06:40.240
Most of the nobility 
look down on adventurers.

06:40.240 --> 06:45.010
How much work has the Green 
Gale done for that noble?

06:45.010 --> 06:46.730
How much work?

06:46.730 --> 06:48.540
To get a recommendation for promotion,

06:48.540 --> 06:50.810
it can't have been just one or two jobs.

06:52.140 --> 06:55.650
As far as I can remember, 
it was only one job.

06:57.020 --> 07:02.480
Now that you mention it, that noble requested 
us, the Blazing Sword, for a job once.

07:02.750 --> 07:06.140
Lightning King was requested for a job as well,

07:06.520 --> 07:07.970
but just that one time.

07:07.970 --> 07:12.360
It seems that this noble is using that 
to see if you'll become allies or not.

07:12.820 --> 07:15.740
There certainly were an 
unusual amount of questions.

07:15.740 --> 07:18.080
They said it was to build 
a closer relationship, but...

07:18.080 --> 07:21.340
Those questions were used to evaluate us?!

07:22.300 --> 07:24.690
Why didn't we notice until now?

07:24.690 --> 07:27.860
Even a seven-year-old child noticed!

07:28.850 --> 07:29.760
<i>Seven-year-old?</i>

07:29.760 --> 07:32.290
I'm not seven! I'm <i>nine</i>!

07:32.290 --> 07:33.950
What? Nine?

07:33.950 --> 07:35.810
You don't look it, though.

07:35.810 --> 07:38.480
Even if I don't look it, I'm nine!

07:38.480 --> 07:43.230
Huh? When we entered town, didn't you 
write that you're eight on the form?

07:43.230 --> 07:48.200
My birthday is at the end of the eighth month, 
so I just happened to turn nine today.

07:48.200 --> 07:51.160
What? In that case, happy birthday!

07:51.160 --> 07:52.120
What?

07:52.120 --> 07:54.200
Yes, happy birthday!

07:54.200 --> 07:55.540
Happy returns.

07:55.540 --> 07:57.030
Happy birthday, Ivy.

07:57.030 --> 07:58.210
Ivy, happy birthday!

07:58.210 --> 07:59.500
Happy birthday, Ivy!

07:59.500 --> 08:01.230
Happy birthday, Ivy.

08:01.230 --> 08:03.090
Happy birthday, Ivy.

08:03.090 --> 08:05.760
Th-Thank you so much!

08:05.760 --> 08:08.980
Next time, let's have a proper
birthday celebration instead of

08:08.980 --> 08:11.220
these meaningless birthday
well wishes, all right?

08:11.220 --> 08:14.440
They aren't meaningless! 
They make me very happy!

08:15.380 --> 08:20.590
<i>How many years has it been since
anyone said "happy birthday" to me?</i>

08:20.590 --> 08:21.920
But, you know...

08:21.920 --> 08:24.230
Are you really nine?

08:24.230 --> 08:25.940
Yes, I am. Why?

08:25.940 --> 08:29.220
From time to time, you seem much older.

08:29.220 --> 08:30.420
That's the truth!

08:30.420 --> 08:34.360
It's hard to believe a nine-year-old
would know so much about cooking, too.

08:36.950 --> 08:39.530
<i>It must be because of my previous life.</i>

08:39.530 --> 08:40.750
Still...

08:40.750 --> 08:44.740
if there's a traitor among the nobility, 
it's going to make things very tricky.

08:44.740 --> 08:47.350
Yes. We'll have to be ready 
for the consequences.

08:47.350 --> 08:49.220
We'll face difficulties on many fronts.

08:49.660 --> 08:51.570
Ivy, I'd like to ask you about something.

08:51.570 --> 08:52.640
What is it?

08:52.640 --> 08:56.910
First, I'd like you to help us consider 
who we should tell about this.

08:56.910 --> 08:59.980
You're thinking that there 
may be even more traitors?

08:59.980 --> 09:03.180
Yes. I was thinking of telling the GM first.

09:03.180 --> 09:07.520
A report on the traitors and on the ones 
who helped to find them, you and Sora...

09:07.520 --> 09:10.970
No, let's leave Sora out of it. 
He's too rare.

09:11.380 --> 09:15.040
Can this "GM" person be trusted?

09:15.040 --> 09:18.790
By "GM," I mean the Guild Master 
of the Adventurers Guild here,

09:18.790 --> 09:20.360
the man in the top spot.

09:20.360 --> 09:22.730
As for being trustworthy or not...

09:22.730 --> 09:24.870
let's investigate that.

09:27.120 --> 09:29.170
This is the Adventurers Guild.

09:32.760 --> 09:35.790
I'll introduce you. He's the Guild Master.

09:36.660 --> 09:38.750
I'm the Guild Master, Rogleef.

09:38.750 --> 09:40.060
You can call me GM.

09:40.450 --> 09:43.180
Pleased to meet you, Mister GM.

09:47.520 --> 09:50.990
I'm the captain of the Watch, Burksby.

09:51.350 --> 09:54.160
Pleased to meet you, Captain Burksby.

09:55.780 --> 09:58.620
I'm the vice-captain, Aggrop.

09:59.010 --> 10:01.830
Pleased to meet you, Vice-Captain Aggrop.

10:04.540 --> 10:07.750
Good. Well, if you'll pardon me 
for just a moment.

10:08.850 --> 10:13.650
Yes. It looks like 
everyone here is all right.

10:13.970 --> 10:16.480
"All right"? What do you mean?

10:16.480 --> 10:19.470
This is a magic item 
that I borrowed from Ivy.

10:19.870 --> 10:23.980
With it, a person can tell if someone 
who has spoken to Ivy is good or bad.

10:23.980 --> 10:27.440
It didn't react, so everyone 
here is on our side.

10:27.440 --> 10:29.780
You have a magic item that does that?

10:29.780 --> 10:32.450
I picked it up in the forest 
during my travels.

10:32.450 --> 10:37.130
But once you use it, it turns into 
a normal stone after about a week.

10:37.130 --> 10:41.470
I had one more, but I used it for 
something silly, and it turned into a rock.

10:41.470 --> 10:44.480
A week. Then, we don't have much time.

10:45.120 --> 10:49.290
Borolda, Ivy, there's something 
I'd like you to use that for.

10:49.290 --> 10:53.180
I know. You mean uncovering members 
of the organization, don't you?

10:53.180 --> 10:54.240
Yes.

10:54.240 --> 10:57.720
I want to find the traitor who passed 
on the information about our investigations.

10:57.720 --> 11:01.260
Can you use that to check 
everyone in the Watch?

11:01.260 --> 11:03.410
We came here with that intent.

11:03.410 --> 11:04.980
We want to check the adventurers, too.

11:04.980 --> 11:07.810
Good! Then, by the authority 
of the Adventurers Guild,

11:07.810 --> 11:10.190
all adventurers will be summoned here!

11:10.190 --> 11:12.360
We will summon all of the Watch as well.

11:12.360 --> 11:13.570
Please give us your help.

11:13.570 --> 11:14.310
Of course!

11:14.310 --> 11:15.030
Yes, sir!

11:20.880 --> 11:24.170
This is the merchant's house that 
the organization was using as their base.

11:24.170 --> 11:26.920
When we raided, it was completely deserted.

11:26.920 --> 11:29.020
For now, to preserve the evidence,

11:29.020 --> 11:31.630
watchmen stand guard while 
we continue to investigate.

11:31.630 --> 11:33.590
Were there any clues?

11:33.590 --> 11:34.990
No, not a one.

11:34.990 --> 11:37.560
It's almost unnatural how 
nothing at all has turned up.

11:41.140 --> 11:43.410
Good work. Let me introduce you.

11:43.410 --> 11:44.970
This child is named Ivy.

11:44.970 --> 11:47.660
Due to certain circumstances, 
we're looking after him.

11:47.660 --> 11:50.020
Ivy, let me introduce these watchmen.

11:50.020 --> 11:51.900
The man on the right is Zakkas.

11:52.210 --> 11:53.320
I'm Zakkas!

11:55.400 --> 11:56.840
On the left is Malgajula.

11:56.840 --> 11:59.610
I'm Malgajula. Pleased to meet you.

12:02.880 --> 12:05.710
I'm Ivy. Pleased to meet you.

12:06.240 --> 12:08.210
It's been a while, hasn't it, Malgajula?

12:08.210 --> 12:10.580
I haven't seen you around, 
but you've been here?

12:10.580 --> 12:14.560
Yeah. We've been looking for evidence 
all this time, but nothing's turned up.

12:14.560 --> 12:16.260
We'll be searching the house today, too.

12:16.470 --> 12:18.180
Really? Well, hang in there.

12:20.610 --> 12:22.320
It can't be. Malgajula?

12:22.320 --> 12:23.680
Yes. He's guilty.

12:23.680 --> 12:26.550
And I trusted him, blast it.

12:26.550 --> 12:28.140
We're only just getting started.

12:28.550 --> 12:30.810
We summoned the whole Watch.

12:30.810 --> 12:32.610
They'll assemble here soon.

12:32.900 --> 12:36.070
We'll dig up every single one of them. 
We're counting on you, Ivy!

12:36.630 --> 12:37.630
Yes, sir.

12:46.580 --> 12:48.270
Good work, Ivy.

12:48.270 --> 12:52.290
I never imagined that just introducing 
myself could be this exhausting.

12:52.820 --> 12:54.500
Of a hundred and fifty-seven watchmen,

12:54.500 --> 12:57.220
thirty eight of them are traitors?

12:57.220 --> 13:01.910
It's unbelievable. This many spies 
have infiltrated the Watch?

13:02.660 --> 13:05.220
No wonder the organization 
gets away whenever we find a lead.

13:05.220 --> 13:08.390
This means that all of our 
movements have been leaked.

13:08.390 --> 13:11.390
Given all this, we can't 
make any careless moves.

13:13.500 --> 13:15.010
Good work, everyone.

13:15.010 --> 13:17.030
Have there been any developments?

13:17.290 --> 13:20.150
Count Faltoria. Lord Foronda.

13:20.150 --> 13:21.490
Has something happened?

13:21.780 --> 13:24.400
I happened to be nearby.

13:24.400 --> 13:28.140
I thought I'd come and check 
the site while I was here.

13:28.140 --> 13:29.320
I see.

13:29.320 --> 13:33.580
I was with Count Faltoria, 
so I accompanied him, that's all.

13:33.580 --> 13:35.460
Oh. And who is this?

13:35.460 --> 13:37.410
This boy is called Ivy.

13:37.410 --> 13:40.590
He was targeted by the organization, 
so we've taken him into our care.

13:40.590 --> 13:43.200
I see. What a charming boy.

13:43.200 --> 13:45.570
I'm Faltoria. A pleasure to meet you.

13:47.620 --> 13:50.350
I'm very pleased to meet you, 
Count Faltoria.

13:52.210 --> 13:54.650
I'm Foronda. Pleased to meet you.

13:56.720 --> 13:58.440
I'm very pleased to meet you.

13:58.780 --> 14:02.740
If you find anything, be sure 
to notify me immediately.

14:02.740 --> 14:04.610
We look forward to hearing good news.

14:08.840 --> 14:10.310
Really?

14:10.310 --> 14:14.350
Count Faltoria is a hero to this town!

14:14.350 --> 14:17.200
What? What are you talking about?

14:17.200 --> 14:18.670
The count is guilty.

14:18.670 --> 14:19.580
What?!

14:19.580 --> 14:22.030
There are traitors among the nobility, too?

14:22.030 --> 14:22.800
Yes.

14:23.180 --> 14:26.630
Though Ivy suspected as much, 
so we aren't surprised by this.

14:26.630 --> 14:28.040
The boy suspected?

14:28.040 --> 14:31.260
If Count Faltoria is part of the organization,

14:31.260 --> 14:34.250
then he's likely the one in control, 
or close to it.

14:35.000 --> 14:38.360
If that's true, then everything makes sense.

14:38.360 --> 14:40.590
The failed raids...

14:40.590 --> 14:43.510
the fact that our allies were killed...

14:43.510 --> 14:46.750
If he's one of the people who directs 
the organization's movements, then I...

14:47.280 --> 14:48.490
Blast it!

14:48.490 --> 14:51.040
I'm the one who gave him that information!

14:51.040 --> 14:53.500
I'm the one who killed our men!

14:53.500 --> 14:55.200
Don't blame yourself!

14:55.200 --> 14:56.450
This isn't your fault.

14:56.450 --> 14:59.210
The ones we should hate are
the members of the organization.

15:01.890 --> 15:02.670
Ivy.

15:03.050 --> 15:05.110
Is there anything else you've noticed?

15:05.110 --> 15:06.440
Well...

15:06.440 --> 15:11.230
The time between our arrival here 
and Count Faltoria's was much too short.

15:11.230 --> 15:13.800
If the count is a member of the organization,

15:13.800 --> 15:15.640
then I don't think that was 
simply by chance.

15:16.070 --> 15:19.650
The traitors among the watchmen 
haven't left their posts.

15:20.010 --> 15:23.140
Then it's possible that someone 
from the organization

15:23.140 --> 15:25.580
is hiding near this base 
to keep an eye on it.

15:25.580 --> 15:28.660
That can't be! Are you saying that 
this whole town is filled with enemies?

15:28.660 --> 15:30.900
It's probably better to think that it is.

15:31.490 --> 15:34.160
It's no wonder we couldn't find any evidence.

15:34.160 --> 15:36.860
They must have taken 
everything out before the raid.

15:36.860 --> 15:38.310
That isn't possible.

15:38.810 --> 15:43.710
There wouldn't have been enough time 
to remove the evidence before our raid.

15:43.710 --> 15:46.070
We have watchmen from 
our side standing guard, too.

15:46.070 --> 15:48.930
The traitors couldn't have secretly
removed anything either.

15:48.930 --> 15:51.440
Then, why hasn't anyone found anything?

15:51.440 --> 15:53.790
You called out the whole Watch 
to investigate, didn't you?

15:53.790 --> 15:58.360
Um, where did Mister Malgajula 
from earlier search?

15:58.710 --> 16:00.910
Huh? Well, he...

16:00.910 --> 16:02.770
Oh! I see what you mean!

16:02.770 --> 16:08.160
Yes. He likely received orders from the 
organization to maneuver behind the scenes.

16:08.160 --> 16:12.270
He may have reported that there were 
no issues in rooms that had issues.

16:12.780 --> 16:15.330
Ivy, are you <i>really</i> nine?

16:15.330 --> 16:18.100
I don't think that's something 
a nine-year-old would think of.

16:18.100 --> 16:19.290
I'm nine!

16:19.290 --> 16:20.250
What?

16:20.250 --> 16:21.840
You're not six?

16:21.840 --> 16:24.000
<i>That's even </i>younger<i> than before!</i>

16:24.690 --> 16:26.970
I'm <i>nine</i>!

16:27.330 --> 16:30.090
Let's head to the room 
Malgajula was in charge of.

16:30.090 --> 16:31.890
We might find something there.

16:35.410 --> 16:36.600
Malgajula.

16:37.590 --> 16:38.310
Yes, sir!

16:38.310 --> 16:42.070
That room doesn't need searching anymore. 
It's unlikely we'll find anything now.

16:42.070 --> 16:44.180
Go and search the storehouse out front again.

16:44.180 --> 16:46.010
Gather up some men and get to it.

16:46.010 --> 16:46.690
Yes, sir!

16:49.750 --> 16:51.370
All right, let's go.

16:53.190 --> 16:56.450
It doesn't matter what it is. We're looking 
for anything that might be a clue.

16:56.450 --> 16:58.880
A list of organization members' names,

16:58.880 --> 17:00.670
or some record of the way the money moves.

17:00.670 --> 17:02.710
That would allow us to trace their crimes.

17:03.830 --> 17:06.800
Even if I look at these numbers, 
I don't know what they mean.

17:07.250 --> 17:12.150
<i>What? "In movies, at times like this, 
there's a trick bookcase"?</i>

17:12.690 --> 17:14.890
I wonder what "movies" are.

17:17.600 --> 17:21.260
<i>What? "That's the only book where 
the corner of the spine is scuffed"?</i>

17:21.260 --> 17:24.060
<i>Does that mean this one 
spot gets touched a lot?</i>

17:24.740 --> 17:26.710
Here we go.

17:34.280 --> 17:36.360
Ow...

17:40.610 --> 17:41.690
A hidden room!

17:41.690 --> 17:43.320
Great work, Ivy!

17:43.320 --> 17:45.030
Well done finding it.

17:45.030 --> 17:46.960
Are you really nine?

17:47.890 --> 17:49.530
I'm really nine.

17:54.610 --> 17:55.810
This is...

17:56.310 --> 17:58.010
This is an incredible sum.

17:58.010 --> 18:00.490
A sum of money that exceeds imagination.

18:00.490 --> 18:04.980
Does this mean that the organization 
is much larger than we've imagined?

18:04.980 --> 18:07.770
This isn't an amount 
that can be quickly moved.

18:08.170 --> 18:11.240
This likely means that leaving it here 
and running was the best they could do.

18:13.100 --> 18:17.190
This is... a record of the 
organization's business dealings.

18:17.520 --> 18:19.710
It's evidence of the kidnappings.

18:19.710 --> 18:22.780
We may be able to close in 
on those who were involved.

18:22.780 --> 18:28.170
So, the organization hid people
around the building to guard this.

18:29.540 --> 18:31.820
What is it, Captain Burksby?

18:32.320 --> 18:33.970
Let's leave all this as it is.

18:33.970 --> 18:37.600
I want the organization to think 
that we haven't found it.

18:37.990 --> 18:39.720
Put everything back 
as it was and pull out!

18:41.120 --> 18:43.980
This has really turned into something huge.

18:43.980 --> 18:45.690
No one's been able to even rest.

18:46.170 --> 18:48.940
The GM, our team leader, the captain...

18:48.940 --> 18:50.610
They've all been in secret meetings.

18:50.610 --> 18:54.240
That's because there are a huge 
number of traitors among us.

18:54.240 --> 18:57.660
They don't want the organization to notice, 
so they can't move in the open.

18:58.030 --> 19:01.870
But thanks to Ivy and Sora, we're 
starting to see our enemy clearly.

19:01.870 --> 19:05.710
That's true. We'll catch everyone 
in the organization, no matter what.

19:05.710 --> 19:06.740
Yes!

19:07.300 --> 19:09.330
But until we do, it's dangerous.

19:09.330 --> 19:12.440
Ivy, please make sure you 
never do <i>anything</i> alone.

19:12.820 --> 19:16.510
If there's somewhere you want to go, 
just tell me. I'll go with you.

19:16.510 --> 19:18.420
Thank you.

19:18.420 --> 19:22.350
In that case, um... 
I do have one favor to ask.

19:27.360 --> 19:30.280
Oh! Magic filled it full of water!

19:30.280 --> 19:32.320
This will make doing the laundry so easy!

19:32.320 --> 19:34.400
It's a magic item.

19:34.400 --> 19:38.500
They're left in washing areas for the 
people who can't use water magic.

19:38.500 --> 19:41.730
Are there many people 
who can't use water magic?

19:41.730 --> 19:42.930
There are quite a lot.

19:42.930 --> 19:47.090
There are also a lot of people who can't 
use cleaning magic or produce fire.

19:47.090 --> 19:49.040
And I can't use water magic either.

19:49.040 --> 19:50.020
What?

19:50.020 --> 19:53.500
Shifale found a water magic item for me.

19:53.500 --> 19:55.720
That's what I use when I cook.

19:55.720 --> 19:57.360
Oh, I see.

19:57.360 --> 19:59.470
Mister Shifale is very kind, isn't he?

19:59.470 --> 20:02.850
I guess he is... as long as 
you don't make him angry.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.870
Well then, I'll get started 
on my laundry now.

20:07.810 --> 20:09.350
Say, Ivy?

20:09.350 --> 20:10.400
What is it?

20:10.920 --> 20:13.200
I've been wondering...

20:13.200 --> 20:16.110
Ivy, are you really a boy?

20:16.490 --> 20:17.490
What?

20:22.540 --> 20:24.200
I'm sorry! Please don't cry!

20:24.200 --> 20:27.170
I'm so sorry for deceiving you.

20:27.170 --> 20:28.930
There's nothing to apologize for!

20:28.930 --> 20:33.840
You were just trying to protect yourself! 
It's more dangerous for girls to travel alone.

20:33.840 --> 20:35.810
Thank you for saying that.

20:36.220 --> 20:39.800
But I had the chance to tell 
all of you and I kept quiet.

20:40.230 --> 20:42.380
You should keep quiet about it 
from now on, too.

20:42.700 --> 20:44.640
And I'll pretend I don't know.

20:45.160 --> 20:46.970
Thank you.

20:46.970 --> 20:49.330
Then let's finish up your laundry!

20:49.330 --> 20:50.100
All right!

20:50.680 --> 20:52.770
Oh, are you doing laundry today?

20:55.110 --> 20:57.470
Ivy, it's been a while.

20:57.870 --> 20:59.460
Yes, it has been a while.

20:59.460 --> 21:01.300
Have you gotten used to Otolwa?

21:01.300 --> 21:04.070
Yes. It's a very large town, isn't it?

21:04.070 --> 21:07.120
It is, and there are 
a lot of fun places to go visit.

21:07.120 --> 21:09.120
Let's explore. 
Won't you come and have fun with me?

21:09.460 --> 21:10.710
Um, I...

21:10.710 --> 21:14.060
That's right! I know a shop 
that has delicious sweets.

21:14.060 --> 21:15.170
What do you think?

21:15.170 --> 21:17.060
Um, well...

21:17.060 --> 21:20.630
It's called Mamaroko. 
Why don't we go together?

21:21.370 --> 21:22.890
Oh, I like the sound of that!

21:23.200 --> 21:24.930
Let's go eat something sweet!

21:24.930 --> 21:27.930
Hold on. Lattrua, I wasn't asking you.

21:27.930 --> 21:31.930
Hey, you know I have a sweet tooth and 
you're going to leave me out? That's mean.

21:32.850 --> 21:35.230
Let's all go together. All right?

21:36.500 --> 21:39.110
It's decided! To Floflo we go!

21:39.110 --> 21:42.580
Why? I was inviting him to go to Mamaroko!

21:42.580 --> 21:46.700
I was just telling Ivy that we 
should go to Floflo sometime.

21:46.700 --> 21:47.840
Right, Ivy?

21:47.840 --> 21:50.000
What? Oh. Yes!

21:51.830 --> 21:52.890
Really?

21:52.890 --> 21:56.250
Then let's all go together. All five of us.

21:56.250 --> 21:57.730
All five of us?

22:00.240 --> 22:02.580
Sounds good. Five of us, then.

22:02.580 --> 22:04.800
It sounds like it'll be a jolly good time.

22:11.000 --> 22:14.590
<i>You are not alone</i>

22:14.590 --> 22:18.150
<i>Open your eyes</i>

22:18.150 --> 22:19.940
<i>That’s the way</i>

22:19.940 --> 22:24.640
<i>You’ll be fine</i>

22:24.640 --> 22:28.720
<i>All of us are here now</i>

22:28.720 --> 22:34.540
<i>You’re something special</i>

22:34.540 --> 22:41.810
<i>Please just relax, and move forward</i>

22:42.800 --> 22:47.220
<i>Because you are here now</i>

22:47.220 --> 22:52.080
<i>The world is so beautiful</i>

22:52.080 --> 22:57.830
<i>This place is full of light</i>

22:57.830 --> 23:04.450
<i>You had countless nights of tears</i>

23:04.450 --> 23:11.840
<i>But you walked all the way here</i>

23:11.840 --> 23:18.160
<i>If it’s dark we’ll be your light</i>

23:18.160 --> 23:27.990
<i>You see the end of this road 
is crystal clear</i>
